; cache-binary.fk — the .fkb fast path, split out of cache.fk 2026-08-14.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/cache.fk
;
; WHY THIS IS ITS OWN CELL. read_with_cache is the only thing in the cache layer
; that reaches read_form_binary / write_form_binary, and those two are native on
; go / rust / ts and ABSENT on fkwu. Because they were named inside cache.fk,
; every chain that preluded cache.fk inherited the absence as two unresolved
; calls — and an unresolved call answers `nothing` quietly under axiom-5, so a
; band's bits that touch one read 0 without the band saying so. Measured
; 2026-08-14: 201 cells across form/ and learn/ name form-stdlib/json.fk or
; form-stdlib/cache.fk while calling nothing from them.
;
; cache-fresh? asks only file_mtime, which every arm has. So the freshness
; predicate stays in cache.fk where anyone can hold it, and the binary door moves
; here where only its two real callers reach for it — concept-corpus.fk and
; i18n.fk, the only cells in the tree that call read_with_cache.
;
; This is the same repair as dropping a dead prelude, made once at the source
; instead of once per consumer: a cell should not hand its callers a door they
; did not ask for and cannot open on their own arm.
;
; Returns a Recipe NodeID. Either re-hydrates from the .fkb (fast path) or runs
; `parse-fn source-path source-text` and writes the result back to the cache.
; `parse-fn` is any (source-path text) -> Recipe function.

(defn read_with_cache (source-path cache-path parse-fn)
    (if (cache-fresh? source-path cache-path)
        (read_form_binary cache-path)
        (do
            (let recipe (parse-fn source-path (read_file source-path)))
            (write_form_binary cache-path recipe)
            recipe)))

0
